.TH NETSTAT 1
.SH NAME
netstat \- the sockets open, and their programs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B netstat
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B netstat
lists the sockets the network server has open (at most 64): TCP or UDP,
our port, the other side's address and port
.RB ( *
when there is none), the TCP state (listen, established, time-wait...)
and the pid of the process that owns it.
.PP
.B netstat
is another name of
.BR fetch (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ifconfig (1),
.BR ps (1),
.BR fetch (1),
.BR netd (4)
